Skip a join's upload when copies from several GPU-modified images overwrite it whole, adapted from
Lichii (github.com/zortos293/Lichii) 6bb6eb4 (#1079). Residual delta over 99zzzz3, which has the
single alias-copy case (CopiesWriteWholeImage, copied_whole).
MarkSubresourcesWrittenWhole (util) sets written[level * layers + layer] for every subresource the
copies write whole (same safety filters as before: 2D, same format and astc_opaque, uncompressed,
no Rescaled, TrimmedLevels, Unbacked or Sparse image, origin offset, full extent); CopiesWriteWholeImage
is now "mark, then all_of" with the same results. JoinImages, at 1x and 1 sample and when no alias copy
covered the image, accumulates the marks of the non-alias GpuModified 1-sample overlaps' shrink copies
(an overlap whose base TryFindBase cannot find is skipped) and sets copied_whole when every level and
layer is marked, so the upload is skipped exactly as for an alias copy. Upstream saw Mario Kart World
render each layer of shadow maps and colour arrays as its own target, then sample the array (13-31 ms
upload an array there); not measured on this build.
diff -ruN a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -2741,6 +2741,27 @@
             break;
         }
     }
+    // Copies from several overlaps the GPU wrote can each write a part of the image, together all
+    // of it: Mario Kart World renders each layer of its shadow maps and colour arrays as a target of
+    // its own, then samples the array. Upstream (Lichii) measured 13-31 ms an array in uploads.
+    if (!can_rescale && !copied_whole && new_info.num_samples == 1) {
+        std::vector<u8> written(
+            static_cast<size_t>(new_info.resources.levels * new_info.resources.layers));
+        for (const JoinCopy& copy : join_copies_to_do) {
+            const Image& overlap = slot_images[copy.id];
+            if (copy.is_alias || False(overlap.flags & ImageFlagBits::GpuModified) ||
+                overlap.info.num_samples != 1) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            const std::optional base = new_image.TryFindBase(overlap.gpu_addr);
+            if (!base) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            const auto copies = MakeShrinkImageCopies(new_info, overlap.info, *base, 1, 0);
+            MarkSubresourcesWrittenWhole(new_image, overlap, copies, written);
+        }
+        copied_whole = std::ranges::all_of(written, [](u8 whole) { return whole != 0; });
+    }
     if (overwritten_by_clear()) {
         // Stays CpuModified: UpdateRenderTargets' PrepareImage drops the upload only when
         // IsFullClear agrees the clear covers the whole image, and uploads it otherwise.
